{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "New Interests and Aspirations"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Emotional Intelligence"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe necessity, duty, advice, or strong dissaproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le04ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Expressing Necessity in the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> to express necessity in the past.<br/> You use the negative forms of the modals <span class=\"italic\">need to </span>and <span class=\"italic\">have to </span>to express absence of necessity in the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can only express necessity in the past with the modal <span class=\"italic\">have to</span>. <br/> <br/>Structure: <br/><ul> subject + had to + infinitive</ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:  <br/> <ul><span class=\"italic\">I was introverted and I <span class=\"strong\">had to survive </span>the first year of university reading a lot of books.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of necessity is expressed with the <span class=\"strong\">negative form of have to</span> in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To express absence of necessity in the past, you use the structure: <br/><br/> <ul>subject+didn't + have/need + infinitive </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><ul><span class=\"italic\">I was outgoing as a kid, so I <span class=\"strong\">didn't have to try </span>hard to be comfortable around people.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of necessity can also be expressed by negative form of need."}, {"type": "example", "content": " You had to go to boarding school at ten."}, {"type": "example", "content": " Did you have to adapt in order to help yourself?"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I had to be around people all the time."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Using Contrast Connectors to  Explain and Supporting Your Ideas"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use contrast connectors to express your position and to show another point of view. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Connectors can show a connection to what you want to say and what was said before. They can also show your position and opinion on a particular situation. <br/><br/> Contrast connectors are usually placed at the beginning of a sentence and provide a contrast with a previous statement or sentence. <br/><br/> Structure:<br/><ul> <span class=\"italic\">Initial Sentence</span>. <span class=\"strong\">Contrast Connector</span>, + <span class=\"italic\">phrase</span>.</ul> <br/><div class=\"center_text\">Look at the chart for some common contrast connectors:</div>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Contrast Connector\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Contrast Connector\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" However\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" On the other hand\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" In contrast\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" By comparison\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Nevertheless\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" On the contrary\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Nonetheless\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Instead\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Yet\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" In any case\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "emotional intelligence"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "understanding of the emotions you and other people experience"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Emotional intelligence is the ability to perceive emotions, self-regulate your own emotions and reflect on your emotional experiences."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about emotional intelligence."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to perceive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to understand; to become aware"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If I understand correctly, emotional intelligence is the ability to perceive emotions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to self-regulate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to control your own feelings and reactions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can self-regulate so you don't react too strongly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "social sphere"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the people you know socially"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Emotional intelligence helps us to navigate our social sphere a little better."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "boarding school"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a school that also provides room and board"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:It was probably tough that you had to go to boarding school at ten."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "introspective"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to see and understand oneself"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was a shy kid and I became pretty introspective."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "self-reflection"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of looking at and understanding your motives and reactions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I spent a lot of time reading, and I began to have a bit more time for self-reflection."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "therapist"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who helps people with psychological matters"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I began to really learn about my emotions by going to a therapist."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to discriminate between"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to tell the difference or decipher between two or more things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My therapist helped me discriminate between my reactions and my ability to control them without compromising my feelings."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le04ob03aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Discuss with a partner how emotionally intelligent you are and why."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go online and find a questionnaire on emotional intelligence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do the test."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your results with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about character traits."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read and answer questions online about my character."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the results with someone."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le04ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le04ob03re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le04ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Will</span>: So, Vanessa, if I understand correctly, emotional intelligence is the ability to perceive emotions, self-regulate your own emotions and reflect on your emotional experiences?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le04ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes. You have the right idea. All in all, it is the way we process emotional information and it helps us to navigate our social sphere a little better. So how about you, Will? It was probably tough that you had to go to boarding school at ten. What was your experience like, and how did it impact your ability to manage your emotions?", "id": 2, "time": "12000", "image": "engenn10le04ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Will</span>: For one thing, I was a shy kid and I became pretty introspective, because the first year at boarding school was lonely. I had one or two friends but I spent a lot of time reading, so I began to have a bit more time for self-reflection.", "id": 3, "time": "34000", "image": "engenn10le04ob03re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: That sounds lonely! What type of strategies did you have to adapt in order to help yourself?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Will</span>: I think I accepted that I was just introverted and that I had to survive the first year or two reading a lot of books.", "id": 4, "time": "51000", "image": "engenn10le04ob03re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: What realization did you come to?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Will</span>: I realized that though I was somewhat introverted, I also craved to be socially involved. That's when I felt I had to try acting and I began to really learn about my emotions, but above all, going to a therapist helped me discriminate between my reactions and my ability to control them without compromising my feelings \u2026 Vanessa, how about you? How did you first learn to manage your emotions?", "id": 5, "time": "65000", "image": "engenn10le04ob03re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I was pretty dramatic as a teenager, and I had to be around people. With respect to self-reflection, I kept a journal and spent time alone cooking. I always took time for myself but knew that my relationships were valuable too.", "id": 6, "time": "93500", "image": "engenn10le04ob03re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about education and character traits."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express what is and isn't necessary in the past."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can accurately explain and support my ideas. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What is your definition of emotional intelligence?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think emotional intelligence is important? Why or why not?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_